  ["Append a &str to the end of a mutable String. Which method?"] = "Añade un &str al final de un String mutable. ¿Qué método?",
  ["Arc shares ownership across threads; Mutex guards changes; atomics count without a lock."] = "Arc comparte el ownership entre threads; Mutex protege los cambios; los atómicos cuentan sin lock.",
  ["Arc, Mutex and atomics"] = "Arc, Mutex y atómicos",
  ["Arc::clone(&sold) bumps the count, never copies the data. Same as sold.clone(), but the full path shows it is cheap."] = "Arc::clone(&sold) sube el contador, nunca copia los datos. Igual que sold.clone(), pero la ruta completa muestra que es barato.",
  ["Arc<Mutex<Receiver<Job>>> is Send + Sync, so it can be moved into every worker. The rail is shared, the pull is exclusive."] = "Arc<Mutex<Receiver<Job>>> es Send + Sync, así que puede moverse a cada worker. El riel se comparte, la extracción es exclusiva.",
  ["Arc<Mutex<T>> is the shared-and-mutable idiom. Arc shares, Mutex guards; neither alone is enough."] = "Arc<Mutex<T>> es el idioma de compartido y mutable. Arc comparte, Mutex protege; ninguno basta por sí solo.",
  ["Arc<T> counts references atomically, so clones may live on different threads. Rc is cheaper but not Send."] = "Arc<T> cuenta referencias de forma atómica, así que los clones pueden vivir en threads distintos. Rc es más barato pero no es Send.",
  ["Arrays, slices, append"] = "Arrays, slices, append",
